---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { organization } from '../lib/seo';
---

<Prose
  title="About Dropzy"
  description="Why Dropzy exists: moving a file between your own devices shouldn’t need an app, an account or a cable."
  heading="Moving a file shouldn’t be a whole process"
>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(organization)} />
  <p>
    You have a photo on your phone and you need it on your laptop. Or a link on your computer that you want on your phone.
    It should take seconds, but it usually means installing an app, signing in to something, emailing yourself, or hunting
    for a cable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Dropzy is the shortcut. Open it on both devices and they find each other. Drop in files or text and they show up on the
    other side — straight across when they can, uploaded for a few hours when they can’t, and deleted automatically either
    way.
  </p>
  <h2>What we care about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Easy.</strong> Opening the page is the whole setup. One obvious next step on every screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Free.</strong> No paid plans and no accounts. Dropzy is built to run on free tiers.</li>
    <li><strong>Private by default.</strong> Everything is temporary, Private Share is end-to-end encrypted, there are no cookies, and we never store IP addresses.</li>
    <li><strong>Lean.</strong> Pages load fast, even on a phone on a slow connection.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who makes it</h2>
  <p>
    Dropzy is a small, independent project. We read every message and feature request — if something could be simpler,
    <a href="/contact">tell us</a>.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/contact">Got feedback? Come say hi.</a></p>
</Prose>
